med_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/630232138","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/1515#issuecomment-630232138","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/1515","id":630232138,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYzMDIzMjEzOA==","user":{"login":"samuelcolvin","id":4039449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzk0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4039449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcolvin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-05-18T14:47:25Z","updated_at":"2020-05-18T14:47:25Z","body":"This has nothing to do with the mypy pydantic plugin (other than that mypy now knows what fields `__init__` takes)\r\n\r\nYou get the same error with\r\n\r\n```py\r\nimport pydantic\r\n\r\nclass Parent(pydantic.BaseModel):\r\n    a: int = 1\r\n\r\nclass Child(Parent):\r\n    b: int = 2\r\n\r\ndef foo(*, a: int, b: int) -> None:\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nfoo(**Parent().dict(), b=3)\r\n```\r\nwithout the mypy pydantic plugin enabled.\r\n\r\nAFAIK this is how how mypy is, it doesn't know anything about the dictionary returned by `.dict()` so it assumes the worst - e.g. that it might include a key `'b'`.\r\n\r\nIt might be possible to extend the the mypy plugin to customise what mypy assumes `.dict()` returns to be a `TypedDict` - if you're interested in working on that I'd happily review a PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/630232138/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"samuelcolvin","id":4039449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzk0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4039449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcolvin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":3347698243,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MzM0NzY5ODI0Mw==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/events/3347698243","actor":{"login":"samuelcolvin","id":4039449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzk0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4039449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcolvin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/follo